# A sound card made of software, for the tests of the audio engine.
#
# snd-aloop is a "cable": what is played on one of its two devices is
# recorded from the other. The ALSA back end of the engine is tried on
# it in a virtual machine, where there is no audio interface (step P1.4;
# choice of the user, 21 November 2026).
#
# A module, never loaded by itself: no hardware asks for it. On a real
# machine it is loaded only by the test that needs it. Everything it
# relies on (PCM, timers) is already built into the kernel, so adding it
# changes no code of the kernel image.
CONFIG_SND_ALOOP=m
